  ("A hash turns any data into a short fixed-length value. A tiny change gives a completely different hash, and you cannot get the original back from it.", "Un hachage transforme toute donnée en valeur courte de longueur fixe. Un minuscule changement donne un hachage totalement différent, et on ne retrouve pas l'original.", "Hash ihindura amakuru yose mu gaciro kagufi kangana buri gihe. Ihinduka rito ritanga hash itandukanye, kandi ntushobora kugarura ayo wari ufite.", "Hash hubadilisha data yoyote kuwa thamani fupi ya urefu usiobadilika. Badiliko dogo hutoa hash tofauti kabisa, na huwezi kurejesha asili."),
